  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN276.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">talaimakaṭkut pāṅkāyiṉār kēṭpat parattai colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What the other woman said so that those near to HER would hear.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN276.1">
        <l>nīḷirum poykai yiraivēṭ ṭeḻunta</l>
        <l>vāḷai veṇpōt tuṇīiya nāraita</l>
        <l>ṉaṭiyaṟi vuṟuta lañcip paiyeṉak</l>
        <l>kaṭiyilaṉ pukūum kaḷvaṉ pōlac</l>
        <l>cāa yotuṅkun tuṟaikē ḻūraṉō</l>
        <l>ṭāva tāka viṉinā ṇuṇṭō</l>
        <l>varukatil lammaveñ cēri cēra</l>
        <l>varivē yuṇkaṇ vaṉpeṇṭir kāṇat</l>
        <l>tārun tāṉaiyum paṟṟi yāriyar</l>
        <l>piṭipayiṉṟu ta<supplied>rū</supplied>um peruṅkaḷiṟu pōlat</l>
        <l>tō<supplied>ḷ</supplied>kan tākak kūntaliṟ piṇittavaṉ</l>
        <l><supplied>mā</supplied>rpukaṭi koḷḷē ṉāyi <supplied>ṉā</supplied>rvuṟ</l>
        <l>ṟirantōrk kīyā tīṭṭiyōṉ poruḷpōṟ</l>
        <l>parantu veḷippaṭā tāki</l>
        <l>varuntuka til<supplied>la</supplied>yā yōmpiya nalaṉē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="6ab">Let happen what will happen</l>
        <l corresp="5cd 2d">with the man from the village by the ghat, where the crane</l>
        <l corresp="1">that had risen to hunt for prey in the long dark pond</l>
        <l corresp="2a-c">in order to eat the white male of the Vāḷai fish</l>
        <l>is afraid that its foot[fall] may be perceived [and], like a robber </l>
        <l corresp="3-5b">who enters softly into a protected house, steps carefully(?).</l>
        <l rend="indent5" corresp="6cd">Is there now shame?</l>
        <l corresp="7">Would that he came!  When [he] joins our quarter,</l>
        <l corresp="9a-c">if I do not grip [his] garland and cloth</l>
        <l corresp="8">for the harsh women to see, [their] kajal eyes covered with red streaks,</l>
        <l corresp="11">fetter [him] with [my] tresses to [my] arm as a stake,</l>
        <l corresp="9d-10">like an elephant bull that the Āriyar bring in by training a female elephant,</l>
        <l corresp="12a-c">[and] take over the protection of [his] chest,</l>
        <l corresp="15">let [my] beauty that mother protected suffer,</l>
        <l corresp="14">as something that does not spread [and] come out,</l>
        <l corresp="12d-13">like the wealth someone amassed without feeling affection [and] giving to beggars.</l>
      </lg>
